  "live_records": {
    "q-39877": {
      "dom_id": "step-q39877",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Find the acute angle between the vector $x$ and the subspace spanned by the linearly independent vectors $\\{{a}_{1},{a}_{2}\\},$ where\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRound the answer to $2$ decimal places.",
      "worked_solution": "The orthogonal projection of $x$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of a matrix $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x=A({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}\\,{A}^{T}\\,x.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,{A}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we get the following projection: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{S}\\,x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {([\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}])}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot {[\\begin{aligned}6 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 9\\end{aligned}]}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3} & \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThe acute angle between $x$ and $S$ is the acute angle between $x$ and ${\\text{proj}}_{S}x.$   \n\nComputing the cosine using the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{x\\cdot {\\text{proj}}_{S}x}{‖x‖‖{\\text{proj}}_{S}x‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot 2+2\\cdot 2+1\\cdot 2}{\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{\\sqrt{14}\\sqrt{12}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{2\\sqrt{42}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{42}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{42}})≈{22.21}^{∘},\n$$\n\nwhich is already an acute angle.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
